      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if the adoptable storage unlocking should just be built into `IVold#unlockUserKey()`, and likewise locking into `IVold#lockUserKey()`.  It doesn\u0027t look like `system_server` needs the flexibility to do anything else.  As you\u0027ve noticed, at a high level a user\u0027s CE storage is meant to be either locked or unlocked.  We never want to have different states on different volumes.  So, just making `IVold#unlockUserKey()` and `IVold#lockUserKey()` do the right thing seems desirable, and then this `StorageManagerService` change would be unnecessary.\n\nNote that `vold` already has access to volume information via its `VolumeManager`; it\u0027s actually where `StorageManagerService` gets it from in the first place!  So, it would be possible for `VoldNativeService::unlockUserKey()` and `VoldNativeService::lockUserKey()` to iterate through the volumes.  (A caveat is that `vold` wants `ACQUIRE_LOCK` to access the `VolumeManager`, but `ACQUIRE_CRYPT_LOCK` to do anything related to crypto.  We\u0027d probably need to collect the list of relevant volume uuids under `ACQUIRE_LOCK`, then process it under `ACQUIRE_CRYPT_LOCK`.)",
